to v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, reports healthy, and its error rate is down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for payments-worker, and on-call was paged. The first attempt to create it timed out. I checked that no incident had been created, then retried with the same idempotency key so it couldn't be opened twice.\n\n**Still failing:** payments-api is still on v5.1.0 and was at an 18% error rate when I checked right after the rollback. It may just need time to recover now that the worker is fixed. If it stays degraded, the next option is rolling it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release. I haven't done that because you said the API errors come from the worker. I added this to the incident summary so on-call can keep an eye on it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UVwGn1ntjNQ2RSdsjidqLG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Px73kBK3tRdePriRTzSs16", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01D5KEXd4EFW9FMoTbu3iLMs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_018ddPoMwvHPcVtngQ1Q1dQs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QivC7jWKqjBaGGemw4iyUb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PJeQX7gLLFDcWtdrsytf1D", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payment"}, "nam