er": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy causing elevated errors", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "This morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0 left the service unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at 18%, which is downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0191mAZNuZZ9vmHN3oy5Qa9v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PXFVbHohy72VY5yct58N4H", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WkzYCgvBbACqiB5Zc6ov8C", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01SXKxo2kZhVTfG5yDHsFT9L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy causing elevated errors", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "This morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0 left the service unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at 18%, which is downstream of the worker. Rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. The worker is now healthy (0.2% errors). payments-api was still at 18% errors right after the rollback and needs monitoring.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001). However, payments-api still has errors after the rollback.\n\n**Rollback:** Both payments services were failing at an 18% error rate. You confirmed payments-worker is the cause, so I rolled it back from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, reports healthy, and its error rate is down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for payments-worker, and on-call was paged. The first attempt to create it timed out. I checked that no incident had been created, then retried with the same idempotency key so it couldn't be opened twice.\n\n**Still failing:** payments-api is still on v5.1.0 and was at an 18% error rate when I checked right after the rollback. It may just need time to recover now that the worker is fixed. If it stays degraded, the next option is rolling it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release. I haven't done that because you said the API errors come from the worker. I added this to the incident summary so on-call can keep an eye on it.", "type": "text"}]}]}